        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>I\u2019ve said it before and I\u2019ll say it again: AI voice modes pretty much suck.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As good as the voice modes for ChatGPT and Gemini are (Claude\u2019s is <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/anthropic-plans-expanding-claude-voice-mode-to-more-languages/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/anthropic-plans-expanding-claude-voice-mode-to-more-languages/\">said to be getting an upgrade soon</a>), they\u2019re basically just reading aloud their lengthy, AI-generated responses to your queries, making you feel like you\u2019re being lectured rather than conversed with.\u00a0</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Another issue is that ChatGPT\u2019s and Gemini\u2019s voiced answers come out of their virtual lips fully formed, meaning they lack the organic quality of human speech that\u2019s composed on the fly and often loops around, meanders, pivots, or even contradicts itself.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Enter Sesa",
